#: ../../source/websocket-extensions_README.md:246
msgid "*ClientSession*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-extensions_README.md:248
msgid ""
"A *ClientSession* is the type returned by `ext.createClientSession()`. It"
" must implement the following methods, as well as the *Session* API "
"listed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-extensions_README.md:259
msgid ""
"This must return a set of parameters to include in the client's `Sec-"
"WebSocket-Extensions` offer header. If the session wants to offer "
"multiple configurations, it can return an array of sets of parameters as "
"shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-extensions_README.md:267
msgid ""
"This must take a single set of parameters from the server's handshake "
"response and use them to configure the client session. If the client "
"accepts the given parameters, then this method must return `true`. If it "
"returns any other value, the framework will interpret this as the client "
"rejecting the response, and will `throw`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-extensions_README.md:273
msgid "*ServerSession*"
msgstr ""

